# Spec Impl Existing Code Preservation Rule

When handling `/kiro/spec-impl`, if implementation requires modification of existing source code, preserve the existing code as the default approach.

- When modifying existing source code, follow the current code structure, naming, and responsibilities unless a change is necessary for implementation, readability, or maintainability.
- Prefer minimal and localized changes over broad rewrites.
- Do not broadly replace existing code when the required implementation can be completed by extending or partially modifying the current code.
- This rule applies only to the `spec-impl` workflow.
